(3517021, 489412, 70375, '<td valign="top">Hi kelly!! I am going to attempt a helping hand here :)<br/> <br/>The first thing I noticed is your DOF. If you are shooting a landscape like this, try a critical f8 or f11. It will pull the whole street into focus.<br/> <br/>Second thing is the really bright whites. Set your ISO to 100 and adjust around it. <br/> <br/>A little advice from someone going through it herself: always shoot at least 20 shots... 10 with your f stop at 8 and various shutter speeds and 10 with your f stop at 11 with various shutter speeds.<br/> <br/>In photoshop CS, if you want to add a lovely border, try the image&gt;canvas size option or make a selection with the rectangular marquee and do edit&gt;stroke. That will get rid of <i>those</i> comments but does little else.<br/> <br/>I hope this helps :)</td>', 'Hi kelly!! I am going to attempt a helping hand here :) The first thing I noticed is your DOF. If you are shooting a landscape like this, try a critical f8 or f11. It will pull the whole street into focus. Second thing is the really bright whites. Set your ISO to 100 and adjust around it.  A little advice from someone going through it herself: always shoot at least 20 shots... 10 with your f stop at 8 and various shutter speeds and 10 with your f stop at 11 with various shutter speeds. In photoshop CS, if you want to add a lovely border, try the image>canvas size option or make a selection with the rectangular marquee and do edit>stroke. That will get rid of those comments but does little else. I hope this helps :)', '2007-04-04 01:35:36.000000', NULL, 0),
